EXTENSION "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_CurseOfTheRhineGorge_Torven" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Torven"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Torven (Chapter Twelve: Curse of the Rhine Gorge, p129): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tec7eb452e349ee44cdcc4c ^"Torven" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Companion"
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int 0, Per +1, Pre –1, Com –1, Str 0, Sta +1, Dex +3, Qik +1"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "24"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Wise One; Animal Ken, Intuition, Latent Magical Ability, Wilderness Sense; Magical Air; Magical Animal Companion, Reclusive"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Brave +2, Loner +2, Loyal to Waldheim +2"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "Wise One 1 (Local)"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Short bow: Init 0, Attack +9, Defense +4, Damage +6 Knife: Init +1, Attack +6, Defense +3, Damage +2 Fist: Init +1, Attack +5, Defense +3, Damage 0"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+2"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1-5), –3 (6-10), –5 (11-15), Incapacitated (16-20)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Animal Ken 3 (wolves), Animal Handling 3 (pigs), Athletics 2 (in forest), Awareness 2 (while hunting), Bows 2 (short bow), Brawl 2 (breaking holds), Charm 1 (peasants), Chirurgy 1 (animals), Faerie Lore 2 (Bright Winter), Forest Lore (Westerwald) 3, High German 5 (Franconian), Hunt 3 (roe deer), Leadership 1 (Waldheim), Magic Lore 2 (herbs), Stealth 3 (in forests), Survival 3 (forests), Swim 2 (rivers), Teaching 2 (wilderness skills), Wilderness Sense 3 (forest)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Plain brown clothing (well made), wolf-fur jerkin, bow"
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "2 (2)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Torven is an unassuming man of average height, with scruffy brown hair and a patchy beard. He takes little care of his appearance. Red-Hame is a wolf, with a distinct ruddiness about the neck and along his back, from which he gets his name."
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 129
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Torven is the unofficial leader of Waldheim, but couldn’t be less suited to the role. The other villagers treat him with reverence because of his ability to speak to and befriend animals, but Torven would rather he was just left alone — he doesn’t get on very well with people, finding it hard to maintain a conversation without running out of things to say. He also tends to make strangers wary, although animals instinctively trust him.\n\nHe much prefers to be out in the deep forest, accompanied by his constant friend Red-Hame, a large wolf who has adopted him. He is also still young, and does not seek the burdens of leadership. Nevertheless, he feels responsible for the villagers and will be the first to come to their defense if they should be threatened. His hunches about danger have saved the villagers more than once from both natural and human disasters.\n\nOn more than one occasion, when Torven has been in sore need of help — such as when facing a fierce animal or the count’s huntsmen — one of the many packs of wolves that prowl in the Westerwald have appeared and helped him. Torven has no control over this Latent Magical Ability, and has learned not to rely upon it; however, it makes him a potent force in the forest. Torven was taught to use a short bow by his uncle, who was a forester under the count of Nassau; he has had no other exposure to Martial Abilities.\n\nRed-Hame is a faerie wolf, with a Faerie Might of 12. He is the messenger of the Winter Court, and expresses its wishes to the villagers of Waldheim through Torven."
    }

}
